
🚀 Day 12 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 1 – Two Sum, one of the most fundamental and widely asked coding interview problems.

This problem helped me strengthen my understanding of Hash Maps (Unordered Map) and how they can be used to reduce the time complexity of search-based problems.

💡 Approach: Hash Map (Unordered Map)

Instead of checking every pair of elements using nested loops, I traversed the array only once. For each element, I calculated its required complement (target - currentElement) and checked whether it already existed in the hash map. If it did, I had found the answer. Otherwise, I stored the current element and its index for future lookups.

Using a hash map reduced the solution from O(n²) to O(n) time complexity.

